137
00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:59.520
Well, this started a whole online petition by office fans.

138
00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:02.280
They started writing in like crazy to NBC.

139
00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:03.920
Give me my remote.

140
00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.060
Northern attack.

141
00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:11.420
And office tally started these online petitions and it was the fans that got us the supersized

142
00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:11.960
episode.

143
00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:12.840
That's great.

144
00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:13.380
And you know what?

145
00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.280
This was before Twitter and Instagram.

146
00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.020
It was not easy to start an online petition back then.

147
00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.040
Yeah.

148
00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:23.600
No, you didn't have the same outreach and they really just like kept at it.

149
00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.880
And NBC was like, okay.

150
00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:26.740
And Greg was thrilled.

151
00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:32.540
Thank you so much to the office fans for making that happen because I could not imagine this

152
00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:33.920
episode being 22 minutes.

153
00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.460
There's so much we would have missed.

154
00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.020
I wish this episode was an hour.

155
00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:38.840
I could have watched even more.

156
00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:44.440
I know, but I kind of feel like that about almost all the episodes, but this one in particular,

157
00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:46.000
I'm so happy with longer.

158
00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.120
That's what she said.

159
00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.140
That's what she said.

