174
00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.500
I mean, seriously, can we talk about this for a second?

175
00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.800
Can we talk about Dunder Mifflin's budget for parties?

176
00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:34.480
I mean, as head of the party planning committee, I usually had some streamers and a cake.

177
00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.940
I mean, and one plastic tablecloth.

178
00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:39.140
It's true.

179
00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:42.540
But then Michael takes us on a booze cruise.

180
00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.820
He throws us this casino night.

181
00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.280
Where is he getting the money for this?

182
00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:51.480
At eight seconds, Jenna, you see them converting the warehouse and there's all these extra employees.

183
00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.660
There's giant neon signs.

184
00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.280
There's dealers.

185
00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.460
I mean, where is this budget coming from?

186
00:07:58.600 --> 00:07:59.600
That I don't know.

187
00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:00.780
That I don't know.

188
00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:08.120
But I did reach out to Kentopedia to find out how we transformed the warehouse into a casino.

189
00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.220
And this is what he said.

190
00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:15.780
He said that he hired a company that specialized in creating casinos for special events like Christmas

191
00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.620
parties or college fundraisers.

192
00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.360
I've been to those things.

193
00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:22.220
Have you I've been to fundraisers that are casino nights.

194
00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:23.260
Yes.

195
00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.660
So there are these companies and they send dealers.

196
00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:26.940
They send all the equipment.

197
00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:32.820
And so he just said he hired one of those companies and then he used all the employees

198
00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.520
from the company as extras in the episode.

199
00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:36.620
What was this budget?

200
00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.160
I'm sorry.

201
00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:40.940
I can't stop talking about the budget, but it was it was crazy.

202
00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:43.700
Do you think we raised more money than the party cost?

203
00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:45.760
No, no.

204
00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:48.040
It was definitely a loss.

205
00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:49.440
It was a loss for sure.

206
00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:53.400
Speaking of the whole casino setup fan question from Explorin Lauren.

207
00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:57.520
She asked in between scenes, did you all play any poker games?

